{
  "description": "Integrate Microsoft Fabric Spark Notebooks as a supported BenchBox platform for\nmanaged Spark-based benchmarking in the Fabric ecosystem.\n\nMicrosoft Fabric Spark is fundamentally different from Fabric Warehouse:\n- **Fabric Warehouse** (existing): T-SQL based, uses COPY INTO for data loading\n- **Fabric Spark** (this TODO): PySpark-based, uses Livy API for job submission\n\nThis fills a critical gap: the existing FabricWarehouseAdapter explicitly notes\nthat Lakehouse data loading requires Spark, which is currently unsupported.\nThis adapter would enable:\n- Full Lakehouse benchmarking with read/write capabilities\n- V-Order optimization (Spark-only feature in Fabric)\n- Delta Lake native operations\n- OneLake integration via Spark paths\n\nKey technical characteristics:\n- Spark 3.4+ runtime with Fabric-specific configurations\n- Livy REST API for remote job submission (notebooks execute remotely)\n- Entra ID authentication (consistent with Fabric ecosystem)\n- OneLake paths: abfss://{workspace}@onelake.dfs.fabric.microsoft.com/...\n- Delta Lake as default table format\n\nReference: fabric_warehouse.py:14-30 documents the Warehouse vs Lakehouse distinction\nand explicitly states Lakehouse requires Spark for data loading.",
  "legacy": {
    "anti_patterns": [
      {
        "dont": "create a local SparkSession",
        "instead": "all Spark code must be submitted as string via POST /sessions/{id}/statements",
        "item_id": "fabric-spark-notebooks-platform",
        "why": "Fabric Spark only runs remotely via Livy API"
      },
      {
        "dont": "duplicate OneLake upload logic",
        "instead": "extract shared OneLake logic to a common internal module",
        "item_id": "fabric-spark-notebooks-platform",
        "why": "fabric_warehouse.py already implements it"
      },
      {
        "dont": "modify fabric_warehouse.py's public interface",
        "instead": "extract shared code to a new internal module if needed",
        "item_id": "fabric-spark-notebooks-platform",
        "why": "it's in production use"
      }
    ],
